id: pm-dkrmzv
title: "GH-787: workspace snapshot and restore primitives for cheap reproducible evaluation episodes"
description: "Provide a supported workspace-level snapshot boundary for agent benchmarks, eval suites, and A/B episodes. Today harnesses must delete and re-seed the complete workspace because item restore and operation-local rollback checkpoints do not capture a whole project. Define authoritative versus derived/transient state and add content-addressed create/restore primitives, or an equivalently complete public SDK contract, so repeated episodes reset safely without stale indexes, copied locks, or hidden external state."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 3
tags[7]: "area:storage",context-management,evaluation,rl,sdk,snapshot,workspace
created_at: "2026-07-28T04:20:29.597Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-28T18:03:04.321Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-28T18:03:01.139Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: "The authoritative workspace snapshot boundary is explicitly versioned and documented, including item files, histories, schemas, extension state, derived indexes, locks, caches, and machine-local state; public SDK and CLI primitives create, inspect, list, restore, and delete named or content-addressed snapshots atomically; restore invalidates or rebuilds derived state and never revives stale locks; unchanged snapshots deduplicate content; repeated evaluation episodes restore faster than full re-seeding at realistic scale; crash safety, cross-version compatibility, multi-branch behavior, security boundaries, and packed installed-consumer tests pass"
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: medium
confidence: 80
resolution: implemented
expected_result: "SDK and CLI consumers can safely snapshot, reset, inspect, and deduplicate authoritative workspace state without stale runtime artifacts."
actual_result: "Versioned content-addressed objects and unambiguous named refs restore through activation-only rollback, report domain errors, and clean stale interrupted publications safely."
