comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-28T04:20:29.597Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence 2026-07-28: all-status searches for workspace-level snapshot, episodic reset, content-addressed restore, checkpoint, and replay found item-level restore/history owners plus reproducible construction feature pm-rbcvt2 and evaluation story pm-nfrhf0, but no workspace snapshot/reset owner. Created as the canonical open GH-787 feature under storage durability; not claimed or implemented in the current PR."
  "2026-07-28T16:27:24.049Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: added SHA-256 content-addressed authoritative workspace snapshots with named references, deduplication, create/list/inspect/restore/delete SDK and CLI operations, clone-local state exclusions, symlink/special-entry rejection, concurrent publish handling, staged atomic swap with rollback, and stale-cache/lock removal. PM-linked unit/integration runs passed 97 lifecycle tests; isolated manual create-mutate-restore verified byte-identical settings; full coverage passed 6,468 tests at 100/100/100/100. Token-surface baseline records workspace help at 90 tokens."
  "2026-07-28T17:06:19.711Z","harness:codex","Review implementation note: restore rollback now covers activation only, missing targets use domain errors, 64-hex reference names are rejected, the schema constant is public, and runtime GC safely removes snapshot publication debris older than 24 hours while retaining active entries."
  "2026-07-28T17:21:31.228Z","harness:codex","Final local review evidence: snapshot CLI/SDK/GC corrections pass focused tests and the full 6,473-test coverage run at exact 100/100/100/100. An isolated fresh-directory manual create-snapshot-mutate-restore verified the original title, exported schema, 64-byte hex identity, and runtime GC dry-run. Static/docstring/token/context/security gates pass."
  "2026-07-28T18:01:30.383Z","harness:codex","Final review evidence: runtime snapshot-temp GC now tolerates ENOENT races after directory enumeration and propagates unexpected stat failures. Dedicated two-branch coverage, focused tests, static quality, and the full 6,474-test exact 100/100/100/100 run pass."
